From eb17af5128fd265bc1c2b2eeba21dc461694e4e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 17:51:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 1.21.28: align Stack page cards, slot rows and stepper
 symmetrically (layout only)

Measured on StackScreen.kt (the rest of the UI's start/end padding is already symmetric):

- Cards on the page used two horizontal gutters: 14 dp (counter row, alignment panel, empty-slot
  placeholder) and 10 dp (master controls, now-playing context card, filled slot cards). With one
  track loaded, a filled card and the empty placeholder directly below it had different widths and
  the card edges zig-zagged down the list. All now use GaSpacing.md (12 dp, a token).
- The empty-slot placeholder used a raw RoundedCornerShape(12.dp) while the filled slot card uses
  GaRadius.control; same component, now the same radius.
- Inside an expanded slot card the buttons row, offset row and volume row used 14/14/18 dp insets.
  Because a TextButton adds its own 12 dp, the visible left edges were about 26/26/18 dp. All rows
  now share the header's 12 dp inset, and the volume label starts at
  ButtonDefaults.TextButtonContentPadding so the three rows share one visible left edge.
- The offset stepper's value was left-aligned next to "-0.1s"; it is now centred between - and +.

Deliberately NOT changed (taste calls that need a screenshot review): Library Add (22 dp) vs Delete
(18 dp) glyph sizes inside equal 48 dp buttons, and the different screen-level gutters (Library 8,
Stack 12, Settings 16, Now Playing 12/16).

Layout-only: no behaviour, permission, decoder or alignment change. Verified: the edited file has no
syntax errors and no off-token horizontal gutters remain in it. Not compiled against the Android SDK
and not rendered or screenshot-tested here.
